# operator_distinct.skill — CDLC Context Package
# KQLBridge v0.1 | Generate → Test → Distribute → Observe
# ============================================================

## What distinct does in KQL
Returns unique rows across the specified columns. `distinct *` deduplicates all columns.

## Translation table
| KQL                        | Spark SQL                         |
|----------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| T | distinct col1, col2     | SELECT DISTINCT col1, col2 FROM T |
| T | distinct *              | SELECT DISTINCT * FROM T          |

## Full examples
```kql
SecurityEvent | distinct EventID, Computer
```
```sql
SELECT DISTINCT EventID, Computer
FROM SecurityEvent
```

## Edge cases
- `distinct *`: `*` is an anonymous terminal in the grammar and is dropped from
  the parse tree → detected by empty children in distinct_op → returns star=True
- distinct after project: DISTINCT applied over the projected columns

## Known limits
- `distinct` with expressions (e.g. `distinct tolower(col)`) → not supported in v0.1

## Routing rules
- distinct_op → SUPPORTED → DistinctOp(star=True or columns=[...])
- Empty children in distinct_op tree → star=True (grammar drops anonymous `*`)
